{"key":"UmlWindow","text":"## UmlWindow\n\nThe **UML Window** is an interactive UML class diagram editor supporting\nsix relationship types, auto-layout, and SAI/Gorp XML import.\n\n---\n\n@layout\nTitle Bar | 0.50, 0.04 | Right-click to rename the window title or save filename. Turns cyan when there are unsaved changes. Save to GitHub persists the diagram; Import loads SAI/Gorp/custom XML.\nClass Box | 0.28, 0.48 | Each class shows Name, Attributes, and Methods sections. Click to select, drag to move, double-click the name to rename. Right-click for: Add Attribute, Add Method, Delete, Connect From Here (starts a relationship).\nRelationship Line | 0.55, 0.42 | Hover to see the relationship type; after 2.5 s a tooltip appears. Right-click to change type or delete. Parallel connections between the same pair of classes are automatically offset by 25 px.\nCanvas | 0.70, 0.70 | Left-drag empty space to pan. Right-click for: Add Class, Auto-Layout (arranges all boxes automatically), Import, Save.\n\n---\n\n### Class Boxes\n\nEach class box has three sections: **name**, **attributes**, and **methods**.\n\n- **Click** to select a class\n- **Drag** to move the class box on the canvas\n- **Double-click** the class name to rename it\n- **Right-click** for the context menu:\n  - Add attribute / Add method\n  - Delete class\n  - Connect From Here (start a relationship)\n\n---\n\n### Members (Attributes & Methods)\n\n- **Double-click** a member to rename it in-place\n- **Drag** members to reorder within the class or move to another class\n- **Right-click** a member for options (delete, change visibility)\n- Visibility icons: `+` public, `-` private, `#` protected, `~` package\n\n---\n\n### Relationships\n\nSix relationship types are supported:\n\n| Symbol | Type | Meaning |\n|---|---|---|\n| ──────▷ | Association | General use/reference |\n| ───────▷ | Dependency | Temporary dependency |\n| ──────▻ | Realization | Implements interface |\n| ──────▷ | Inheritance | Extends class |\n| ◇──────  | Aggregation | Has-a (weak) |\n| ◆──────  | Composition | Has-a (strong, owned) |\n\n- **Connect From Here** — right-click a class, choose *Connect From Here*, then click the target class\n- Hover over a relationship line to see its type label; after 2.5 s a tooltip shows the full description\n- Parallel connections between the same two classes are automatically separated by 25 px\n- Multiplicity labels appear along relationship lines (e.g. `1`, `0..*`)\n\n---\n\n### Canvas\n\n- **Left-drag** empty canvas to pan\n- **Right-click** canvas for: Add Class, Focus, Layout, Window, Import, Save\n- **Layout** submenu — every entry has a tooltip saying what it will do: **Auto-Layout** (the default for a file with no saved positions), **Force-Directed** (connected boxes pull together, every box pushes its neighbours away), **Tree** (layers by inheritance), **Grid** (rows and columns in document order, as many columns as the window is wide), **Fit** (pulls every box into the part of the canvas you can see, bumping the ones already inside to make room) and **Full** (spreads the boxes out from their centre to fill the view, each stopping at the edge or at a box already there)\n- **Window** submenu — on every window's title-bar menu, not only here: **View Extents** (moves all four edges of the window in or out to hug the diagram), **Full Screen** / **Restore Size**, **Minimize**, the halves and quarters of the desktop, and **Center**\n\n---\n\n### File Operations\n\n- **Save** — serialises the diagram to XML and saves to GitHub\n- **Auto-save** — closing or minimizing the window, or hiding the browser tab, saves unsaved changes to the same file\n- **Import** — loads from a SAI XML, Gorp XML, or custom UML XML file\n- Files are loaded from GitHub or StreamingAssets fallback on open\n\n### Status: Stable\n### Purpose: AIDesign\n\n---","screenshot":""}